SUMMARY
The user asked Claude to learn this 2017 Sinatra + AngularJS app and get it running locally. Claude
mapped the codebase, found that bridge "Go" links were ~33 km off because coordinates are packed
degrees-minutes-seconds, and got the app booting on Ruby 3.4.8. The user then set an "every change is
an issue plus a PR" rule in CLAUDE.md, and the session shipped seven merged PRs: the Ruby boot fix,
the CLAUDE.md rule, the bridge-coordinate fix, GitHub Actions CI, a full rewrite in Next.js 16 +
Tailwind CSS 4 + SQLite (Drizzle ORM), and a conversion of the source data to CSV. It ended with
Claude creating a project-level historian-agent (PR #13, open at the time of writing) and running it
to produce this first log.

