DECISIONS AND RATIONALE
- Workflow: every committed change starts with a GitHub issue and lands through its own PR on a
  `<type>/<issue#>-<slug>` branch (CLAUDE.md). The user waived the issue for the historian work.
- Local-run fixes were kept minimal (3 files) rather than upgrading to Sinatra 4, because
  sinatra-assetpack blocked upgrades and the goal was just to run the app.
- Bridge coordinates: raw `ddmmss.ss` fields kept untouched; decoded decimal fields added
  alongside. Values outside NJ bounds become null rather than a wrong pin.
- Stack for the rewrite: Next.js 16 App Router (TypeScript) for UI and API, Tailwind CSS 4
  (chosen over shadcn/ui and Mantine for full control and a small bundle while keeping the
  Bootstrap-era look), SQLite via Drizzle ORM with the libSQL client, Vitest for tests.
  package.json uses "type": "module" so tsx supports top-level await.
- Data import is a Drizzle migration (0001) generated by a committed script from data/source/;
  never hand-edit it, and new data goes in a new migration.
- Bridge source data rebuilt from the original January 2017 export in git history to undo Excel
  damage; the source CSVs keep NJDOT values verbatim and all cleanup lives in tested code.
- Structure-number search normalizes case, non-alphanumerics and leading zeros on both sides.
- Bridge search runs server-side with the query in the URL so Enter, Back and shareable links work.
- The embedded Google map is optional and renders nothing without a key; directions/place links
  use Google Maps URLs that need no key. The Maps key lives only in gitignored local files and
  should be restricted to HTTP referrers and the Maps JavaScript API in Google Cloud.
- robots disallows all crawling, since this is an internal NJDOT staff tool (as before).
- History: after each merged PR, Claude should recommend running the historian-agent; each log
  is committed through its own PR.

FINDINGS AND GOTCHAS
- Bridge lat/lng in the NJDOT export are packed DMS (DD.MMSSss): 40.453661 is 40°45'36.61" =
  40.760169. ~98% of records use this format; 7 are already decimal (4 detectable by minutes >= 60,
  3 need an explicit list); 10 decode outside NJ; ~40 more have wrong coordinates that still fall
  inside NJ (e.g. a placeholder copied across Garden State Parkway structures). Some groups share
  identical coordinates (13 bridges at one point).
- A later Excel re-save of bridges.txt stripped leading zeros from 1,245 structure numbers and
  turned 42 into scientific notation (043E007 -> 4.3E+08). Never re-save the source CSVs in Excel.
- The export encodes apostrophes as underscores in bridge names (BERRY_S, GOV_T); others such as
  RAMP_K are ambiguous and left as-is.
- Original source files were tab-separated .txt with bare-CR line endings and a `Latitutde`
  header typo; one station (Hamilton State Police) has no coordinates; some station hours span
  two lines.
- Old app quirks: case-sensitive substring bridge search, Enter did nothing, empty search loaded
  all 6,540 rows, stations page spun forever without a location answer and never showed hours,
  fuel type or phone; files were opened per request without closing.
- Ruby 3.4.8 boot blockers: lockfile forced Bundler 1.13.7 (crashes on `untaint`), Fixnum removed
  in Ruby 3.2 (sinatra 1.4.7, backports 3.6.8), no bundled WEBrick, and Sinatra 1.4 picking the
  wrong root on Ruby 3.3+ (500 on `/`, 404 on public files).
- macOS AirPlay Receiver occupies port 5000; the Sinatra app used 4567 and the Next app 3000.
- Next 16: PageProps/LayoutProps come from `next typegen`, so `tsc` fails on a clean checkout
  unless typegen runs first (caught only by CI). error.tsx should call retry(), not reset().
- An empty `DATABASE_URL=` crashed libSQL with URL_INVALID; now treated as unset.
- ESLint's react-hooks rule flags any top-level function named use*, even in tests.
- npm 11 skips unapproved install scripts (esbuild, unrs-resolver) but the tools still worked.
- GitHub will not render bridges.csv (724 KB) as a table; stations.csv renders fine.
- Background servers stopped when the session restarted and when the code-review agent ran;
  a stale Next server once held port 3000 (EADDRINUSE).
- The Chrome extension was not connected, so UI checks used headless Playwright screenshots.
- A newly added project agent in .claude/agents/ is not available as a subagent type until the
  session picks it up, so the first log was written by a general-purpose agent following its body.
- The `code` CLI is not on PATH on the user's Mac (fix: VS Code command palette, "Shell Command:
  Install 'code' command in PATH").

